\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My heart is resting, O my God,
\par I will give thanks and sing:
\par My heart is at the secret source
\par Of every precious thing.
\par Now the frail vessel Thou hast made
\par No hand but Thine shall fill;
\par For the waters of the earth have failed,
\par And I am thirsty still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I thirst for springs of heavenly life,
\par And here all day they rise;
\par I seek the treasure of Thy love,
\par And close at hand it lies;
\par And a new song is in my mouth,
\par To long-loved music set-
\par Glory to Thee for all the grace
\par I have not tasted yet;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Glory to Thee for strength withheld,
\par For want and weakness known,
\par And the fear that sends me to Thy breast
\par For what is most my own.
\par I have a heritage of joy,
\par That yet I must not see;
\par But the hand that bled to make it mine
\par Is keeping it for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My heart is resting, O my God,
\par My heart is in Thy care;
\par I hear the voice of joy and health
\par Resounding everywhere.
\par Thou art my portion! saith my soul,
\par Ten thousand voices say,
\par And the music of their glad Amen
\par Will never die away.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

